# This script is expected to be called xx-$app
# shellcheck disable=SC2154 # domain and YNH_STDRETURN are provided by the YunoHost hook-calling context

# The XMPP service subdomains (conference./pubsub./upload./proxy.) are intentionally
# NOT added to the domain's Let's Encrypt certificate.
#
# They have no nginx server block of their own, so their HTTP-01 acme-challenge
# cannot be served (it 302-redirects to the portal). Because YunoHost fails the
# WHOLE cert request if any single SAN fails validation, listing them here breaks
# `yunohost domain cert install` entirely and leaves the domain on a self-signed
# cert. ejabberd presents the main-domain cert for these components via SNI, which
# clients tolerate for normal use.
#
# TODO: to give the subdomains their own valid certs (needed for strict s2s MUC
# federation from remote servers), first add nginx server blocks for them that
# serve /.well-known/acme-challenge/, then re-add the relative names here.

exit 0
